  "id": "autonomic",
  "term": "autonomic",
  "definition": "In counselling and psychotherapy contexts, autonomic refers to body-state regulation linked with arousal patterns such as activation, calming, or shutdown. Changes in autonomic state can affect whether a person stays within a workable range for thinking, feeling, and relating during therapy.",
